WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:07.830
We are back.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:08.830
The first question in the review exercise
asked which assert method is needed to fulfill

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.059
the request on line 8.

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:17.310
We have a value within the list of values,
so we need an assertIn test, which I will

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:22.380
build to replace the comment on line 8.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:35.010
Secondly, the review exercise asked if the
test would pass or fail.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:40.190
I hope that you entered the code needed for
the test and then ran the test because, if

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:45.469
you did that as I am doing here, you would
find that the test failed.

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:52.680
The third question asked you to identify the
cause of the failure if one existed.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:01:02.399
Vilnius, the capital of Lithuania, has a capital
V in variable a, but is all lowercase in variable

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:03.399
b.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:10.980
Remember, values are case-sensitive in Python,
so these two values are different, which is

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.530
why the test failed.

